caption: Blood of the Dragon
tradition-component: blood-of-the-dragon

The practitioner may select and use up to two different Jutsu during one action cycle instead of only one. This explicitly overrides the universal one-Jutsu-per-action selection limit and applies to all Jutsu the character can legally use, regardless of Jutsu Tradition or Domain. It grants no additional maneuver, attack, defense, reaction, Extra Attack, or other action. Each Jutsu must still satisfy its own written cadence and delivery requirements. Two Jutsu may ride the same underlying action only when that action legally satisfies both techniques; otherwise the practitioner needs whatever attacks, reactions, or other actions their written deliveries require. Blood of the Dragon does not allow a character to swing a sword twice, make a second unarmed strike, or otherwise duplicate an action unless they already possess an appropriate source of additional attacks or actions.
